WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:15.420
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon,

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.810
is based on the George RR Martin's Targaryen
history book Fire &amp; Blood.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.390
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.490
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:33.750
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.820
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.379
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:46.840
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.449
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:56.569
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:56.569 --> 00:01:01.309
In other words it covers events from Aegon's
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:05.390
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.320
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.440
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.580
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
When people speak about Aegon's conquest,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.140
people always speak how it's Aegon and his
sister-wives Rhaenyra and Visenya who conquered

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.080
and united the Seven Kingdoms,
but they forget to mention their half-brother

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.670
born out of wedlock, Orys Baratheon.
Son of Aerion Targaryen, Orys played just

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.890
as big role in Aegon's Conquest.
He might not have ridden a dragon (which he

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.920
most certainly would have
if there had been a fourth dragon as he was

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.530
the blood of a dragon himself)
but he commanded Aegon's armies on the ground.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:54.320
As Aegon the Conqueror said it himself, Orys
was his shield, his stalwart, his strong right

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.740
hand.
Why was Orys a Baratheon and not a Targaryen

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.420
you may ask.
Well, Orys and Aegon had the same father,

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.770
Aerion Targaryen, but different mothers,
and unlike Aegon's mother, Orys' mother did

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.920
not wed their father,
therefore Orys couldn't get a Targaryen surname

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.510
as he was born out of wedlock.
How and why did Orys get Baratheon surname

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.450
is unknown,
but it's likely that Baratheon surname was

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.989
used in Valyria for children born out of wedlock
like Snow, Sand and a few more are used for

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:29.080
children born out of wedlock in Westeros.
Lord Orys Baratheon was the founder of House

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.819
Baratheon,
and was half-brother of King Aegon I Targaryen.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:38.189
That's right, first Baratheon was blood of
the dragon, half Targaryen himself.

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:42.749
Orys was one of Aegon's fiercest commanders,
and was regarded as Aegon's only true friend

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:45.840
and champion of his youth. During the War
of Conquest,

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.030
he was a commander in the army of Aegon the
Conqueror.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.999
When Aegon invaded Westeros, he sent Orys
to seize Storm's End,

00:02:52.999 --> 00:02:57.310
the ancestral seat of the Storm Kings and
capital of the Stormlands.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:02.110
Orys defeated the Storm King, Argilac the
Arrogant, and took not only Storm's End,

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:07.700
but also his sigil (the crowned black stag)
and words ("Ours is the Fury"), as well as

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.529
his daughter Argella, and his sword, to cement
his rule over the Stormlands.

00:03:12.529 --> 00:03:15.980
He became the first Lord Paramount of the
Stormlands.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.879
Orys is also considered the first Hand of
the King, serving Aegon the Conqueror.

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:25.690
Famed for his prowess in battle, his commanding
skills and his strong loyalty to King Aegon

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:31.270
I and House Targaryen, Orys was described
as a fierce warrior, fighting for House Targaryen

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:36.200
during Aegon's Conquest, the First Dornish
War, and the Vulture Hunt.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.329
Being the founder of House Baratheon, Orys
Baratheon is the distant ancestor of King

00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:46.549
Robert Baratheon and his brothers, Stannis
and Renly. Orys had black hair and black eyes,

00:03:46.549 --> 00:03:50.309
as well as black beard.
In Game of Thrones, if you paid close attention,

00:03:50.309 --> 00:03:54.299
you could notice that he has an entry in The
Lineages and Histories of the Great Houses

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:58.590
of the Seven Kingdoms. It reveals Orys's marriage
to Argella,

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.629
and that one of his sons died stopping an
assassination attempt

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:07.439
against the son of his half brother Aegon
the Conqeuror, King Aenys Targaryen.

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:12.290
Little is known about his youth, but what
is known is that Orys was Aegon's champion.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.690
When King Argilac Durrandon offered Aegon
his daughter Argella in marriage and some

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:20.030
lands
as her dowry, the Lord of Dragonstone, Aegon

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:25.690
spurned the Storm King's proposal.
Instead, he requested significantly more land

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:29.510
and offered to seal the pact by wedding Orys
to Argilac's daughter.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:34.230
The Storm King angrily rejected these terms,
for Argilac the Arrogant believed that this

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:39.410
was supposed to be an insult for Orys might
have been Aegon's brother and have Targaryen

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.300
blood,
but Orys was a born out of wedlock

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.710
and the Storm King viewed such a match would
dishonor his daughter.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:50.550
Angered at the insult of being offered a man
born out of wedlock instead of a king,

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:55.790
Argilac cut off the hands of Aegon's envoys.
When Aegon's Conquest's had begun, Orys had

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:00.970
command on the ground during the first battle,
defeating Lords Mooton and Darklyn.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.570
Orys led the army while Aegon attacked from
the skies.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:09.000
After Aegon's coronation at Aegonfort, Orys
was raised to Hand of the King.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.750
Within days of the coronation, Orys and Queen
Rhaenys Targaryen, with her dragon Meraxes,

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:19.940
were then tasked with capturing Storm's End,
taking the greater part of Aegon's host with

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.740
them.
While King Argilac gathered his banners,

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.810
Lords Fell, Buckler, and Errol ambushed the
advance elements of Orys's host,

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.400
until they were forced to retreat when Meraxes
burned the surrounding woods.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.980
Argilac the Arrogant, hearing of the burning
of Harrenhal,

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:39.200
knew his formidable walls would not protect
him from dragonfire.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.340
Argilac rode out with his great host to give
open battle and die with a sword in hand.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:49.141
Orys was made aware of Argilac's march by
Rhaenys, who provided him with the Storm King's

00:05:49.141 --> 00:05:53.500
numbers and dispositions, for she had spotted
the host with her dragon.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.760
Baratheon took up a strong position on the
hills south of Bronzegate,

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:01.320
digging in on the high ground while he awaited
the stormlanders.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:06.820
Argilac's host was twice the size of Orys's,
and when the battle called the Last Storm

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:09.310
begun,
the stormlanders managed to break through

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:13.900
the Baratheon center,
only to be engulfed by dragonflame. With Meraxes

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:19.690
and Rhaenys turning the battle into chaos,
Orys descended down the hill, where he encountered

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.710
the Storm King.
Ordering his own men to stand aside, he gave

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:29.440
Argilac a chance to yield.
Argilac cursed Orys and they fought instead.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.660
Although he took wound, Orys slew Argilac
the Arrogant, ending the reign of the Storm

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.320
Kings. The loss of their king made the stormlanders
surrender or flee.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:44.330
After the battle, Argella Durrandon, the daughter
of Argilac, declared herself the Storm Queen

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:48.880
and continued to hold Storm's End until her
household turned against her

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:54.050
to avoid the same fate of Harrenhal. They
delivered her to Orys, naked and chained.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:59.340
Orys, however, covered her with his cloak
and treated her chivalrously.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:04.200
Aegon rewarded Orys with the lands and incomes
of Storm's End and named him Lord Paramount

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:09.260
of the Stormlands. None dared suggest that
he was unworthy of these honors.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:12.520
Orys took Argella as his wife and to honor
Argliac's valor,

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:18.940
he adopted the stag banner, honors and words
of the Durrandons, "Ours is the Fury", forming

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:25.200
House Baratheon. Orys later joined King Aegon
I in the First Dornish War in 4 AC,

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.300
leading an assault on the Boneway with one
thousand picked knights.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.980
His horses struggled up the stony, narrow,
and twisty paths,

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:37.460
while his knights were hit with boulders from
above, the work of defenders the stormlanders

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:41.670
never saw.
Cunning Dornishmen then launched a night raid,

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:46.800
raining arrows, rocks, and spears from above
as the stormlanders crossed a bridge. Bodies

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:52.160
of the invading army blocked the Boneway from
both ends, and when Lord Orys ordered his

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.300
men to fall back, a triggered rockfall cut
off their retreat.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:00.510
With no way forward or back, the stormlanders
were massacred,

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:05.180
save for Orys and a dozen other lords thought
worth the ransom.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:09.630
However, Orys and his bannermen found themselves
the captives of the Wyl of Wyl

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:14.121
the savage mountain lord called the Widow-lover.
When Aegon eventually agreed to the Dornish

00:08:14.121 --> 00:08:18.940
ransom demands, Lord Baratheon and his bannermen
were ransomed in 7 AC

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:23.680
for each man's weight in gold. However, they
were freed only after having their sword hands

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:27.910
chopped off so they would not be able to use
them again against Dorne.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:33.620
Thereafter Orys became known as Orys One-Hand.
In retaliation for this treachery, King Aegon

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.260
descended on the mountain fastnesses of House
Wyl

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.530
with his dragon Balerion and burned them to
rubble,

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:44.650
although the Wyls managed to take refuge in
their caves and tunnels beneath the mountains.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.710
After the loss of his hand in the First Dornish
War, Orys became bitter,

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:52.440
turning his attention to Dorne and obsessed
with the idea of revenge.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:55.660
He resigned his office as Hand and returned
to the stormlands.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:00.910
While resinging, he said to Aegon ''The King's
Hand should have a hand. I will not have men

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.880
speaking of the King's Stump.'' He became
obsessed with vengeance against the Dornish,

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:09.160
especially House Wyl, whose lord had removed
his hand.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:13.890
When Princess Deria Martell came to King's
Landing to provide peace terms,

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:18.460
Lord Orys argued for sending the princess
back to her father Nymor, the Prince of Dorne,

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:22.440
without a hand, but Aegon made peace with
Dorne instead.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:27.350
Orys received his opportunity for vengeance
against the Wyls in the Second Dornish War,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.130
during the early reign of Aegon's son, King
Aenys I Targaryen.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.200
In 37 AC, a Dornish outlaw known as the Vulture
King

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.270
led a huge army to reave the lands north of
the Red Mountains.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:44.330
The Vulture King split his host, having one
half led by Lord Walter Wyl.

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:48.100
The Lord of Storm's End, Orys, eager for revenge
against the Dornish,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.840
led his forces from Storm's End one last time
to participate in the Vulture Hunt.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:58.990
While Wyl's host sat besieging Stonehelm,
Orys's forces crushed the Dornishmen beneath

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.810
the walls of the castle.
Lord Walter Wyl, the son of Wyl who chopped

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:06.530
off Orys' hand, was brought to Orys, wounded,
but alive.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:11.690
''Your father took my hand. I claim yours
as repayment.'' Orys said to him, but he took

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:15.590
far more.
Lord Baratheon chopped off Walter's sword

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.690
hand, then his other hand, followed by both
feet,

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:24.500
which he called his "usury" or in other words,
his prolonged revenge with interest at unreasonably

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.890
high rates.
On his trip home to Storm's End, legendary

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.150
Orys died of the wounds he had taken in the
battle.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:36.060
Orys died content, according to his son Davos,
smiling that he got his revenge.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:40.130
Orys Baratheon, blood of the dragon played
a huge role in Aegon's Conquest,

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:43.030
and is one of the most important characters
from this time period.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:47.290
An honorable man who upholds his loyalty to
his half brother Aegon

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:51.510
and whose prowess in battle was greater even
of that of Aegon himself

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.510
which he proved in the war against the last
Storm King,

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.060
and whose commanding skills earned Aegon the
Conqueror

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:02.029
quite a few important victories in Westeros.
Can we just take a moment to say that this

00:11:02.029 --> 00:11:07.550
Baratheon crown suits Henry Cavill very well.
Huge, strong man with black hair and good

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:11.529
swordmanship, like a true Baratheon.
Perfect choice for Orys Baratheon.

00:11:11.529 --> 00:11:12.529
Let me know your thoughts about all of this
in the comment section down below.

00:11:12.529 --> 00:11:16.640
Thank you so much for watching and hope to
see you in the next one.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:17.300
Peace!

